From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: use a cmake release with a riscv64 wheel

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64-only: PyPI's cmake==3.24.2 ships no riscv64 wheel; this repo already publishes riscv64 wheels of the same scikit-build/cmake-python-distributions project for newer releases]

python/setup.py's CMakeBuild.install_deps() downloads its own cmake
binary from PyPI rather than using any cmake already on PATH, and
3.24.2 predates every riscv64 wheel of that project. 3.31.6 is the
closest release this repo already hosts for manylinux_riscv64;
python/CMakeLists.txt's and the top-level CMakeLists.txt's
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION ...22) upper bound caps the policy set
applied, so a newer real cmake binary changes no build behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 python/setup.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/python/setup.py b/python/setup.py
index 11aca64..34ac7dd 100644
--- a/python/setup.py
+++ b/python/setup.py
@@ -240,7 +240,7 @@ class CMakeBuild(build_ext):
         try:
             self.cmake_log(f"CMake: Extension: {ext.name} Install Deps: Download")
             output1 = subprocess.run([sys.executable, "-m", "pip", "download",
-                                      "cmake==3.24.2", "nanobind==2.9.2"],
+                                      "cmake==3.31.6", "nanobind==2.9.2"],
                                      cwd=ext.builddir,
                                      stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                                      stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
